{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe project pins Opus 4.8, Sonnet 4.6 and Haiku 4.5 (`rebar.toml` `[llm]` and `[llm.model_classes]`, `.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml`, `.github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml`). Bedrock in account 896586841071/us-east-1 serves `us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5`, `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5` and `us.anthropic.claude-haiku-5-5` (ACTIVE in `aws bedrock list-inference-profiles --profile frontier --region us-east-1`). The parent epic requires this upgrade to land first, on the current 4-pass engine.\n\nA bare id swap is unsafe. On 5.5: forced `tool_choice` `any`/`tool` returns 400 (Opus, Sonnet); thinking cannot be disabled (Opus); non-default `temperature`/`top_p`/`top_k` return 400; assistant prefill returns 400; `effort` defaults to `medium` on Opus and Haiku, one level below the `high` that Opus 4.8 and Sonnet 4.6 run at today. The installed runtime does not know these models: `pydantic-ai-slim` 1.107.9 (1.107.10 is security-only) derives Claude profiles in `pydantic_ai/profiles/anthropic.py::anthropic_model_profile` from prefix lists ending at `claude-opus-4-8`, so for `claude-opus-5-5` it reports forced tool choice supported, effort unsupported and sampling allowed — all wrong.\n\n## Approach\n\nSwap the ids, correct the request surface at the seams rebar owns, and prove it on the wire.\n\n**Riskiest assumption first.** rebar's calls carry no forced tool choice, thinking toggle or prefill, so only sampling and effort need code. Code supports it: `structured.output_mode` (`src/rebar/llm/structured.py:149`) returns only `NativeOutput` or `PromptedOutput`; `capabilities._REBAR_OVERRIDES` (`src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py:214`) pins Claude to `native_structured_output=False`, so Claude always takes `PromptedOutput` (no tool, no prefill); no caller sets `RunRequest.thinking=True` (`src/rebar/llm/runner.py:93`); agentic loops leave `tool_choice` at `auto`. Step 1 tests this on the wire before other edits: `python -m rebar.llm.evals.provider_parity --probe` (`provider_parity.py:589`) against each 5.5 slot, recording any 400.\n\n**Ids and tables.** Replace 4.x ids with the 5.5 ids verbatim (direct `claude-opus-5-5`, `claude-sonnet-5-5`, `claude-haiku-5-5`; Bedrock `us.anthropic.*-5-5`, no suffix) in the three toml files, `config.DEFAULT_MODEL`/`VERIFIER_DEFAULT_MODEL` (`src/rebar/llm/config.py:61,67`), `model_classes.TRIVIAL_DEFAULT_MODEL` and `MODEL_WINDOW_LADDER` (`src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py:45,62-66`; Haiku 5.5 window 1M), `review_kernel/verify.py::MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS` (`:294-297`; Haiku 5.5 128K), `bedrock_model.DEFAULT_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` (`:22`), `provider_parity.CLASS_SLOTS` (`:103-106`), `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:97-99` and `infra/terraform/monitoring_eb6e.tf` dimensions. `sizing._RUNG_CLASSES` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py:240`) keys on family substrings and needs no change; a test pins it.\n\n**Sampling.** Add each 5.5 id (bare, `us.`, `global.`) to `_MODEL_ID_CAPABILITY_OVERRIDES` (`capabilities.py:223`) with `supports_temperature: False`, the mechanism already used for Opus 4.7/4.8, so `structured_run.build_model_settings` (`:400-404`) omits Pass-2 `temperature=0`.\n\n**Effort, explicit.** One per-model table beside the overrides: `high` for Opus 5.5 and Sonnet 5.5 (today's effective level), `medium` for Haiku 5.5 (its default). `structured_run.build_model_settings` and `agent_call.build_agent_kwargs` send it through provider-scoped keys: `bedrock_additional_model_requests_fields={\"output_config\": {\"effort\": ...}}` on Bedrock, `anthropic_effort` on direct Anthropic. pydantic-ai honours `anthropic_effort` only when the profile says so, so the direct profile is corrected at rebar's provider seam (`providers.py` `provider_factory`, `:136`): for 5.5 ids it reports adaptive thinking, effort, `anthropic_supports_forced_tool_choice=False` and `anthropic_disallows_sampling_settings=True`, which also makes any future forced tool degrade to `auto`.\n\n**Cache minimum.** Add the three direct 5.5 ids to `_MODEL_CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS` (`capabilities.py:38`) at 512.\n\n**Audit.** Walk every model call site (`runner.py`, `structured_run.py`, `agent_call.py`, `anthropic_model.py`, `bedrock_model.py`, `providers.py`, `review_kernel/`, `plan_review/passes.py`, `workflow/`) against the five changes plus the `refusal` stop reason, and record one row per check (site, finding, fix or \"not affected\") as a ticket comment. Anything needing more than these seams is filed as a bug linked `discovered_from`.\n\nThese seams already shape every call, so correcting them corrects every pass without touching the passes. The eval-spec `model:` pins move in the sibling task `real-pubescent-turnstone` (see links).\n\n## Scope\n\n- rebar.toml, .github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml, .github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml\n- src/rebar/llm/config.py, model_classes.py, capabilities.py, structured_run.py, agent_call.py, providers.py, bedrock_model.py\n- src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py\n- src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py, src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/provider_parity_results.json\n- infra/compose/docker-compose.yml, infra/terraform/monitoring_eb6e.tf\n- tests/unit/test_capabilities.py, test_model_classes.py, test_llm_provider_factory.py, test_project_default_provider.py\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: each 5.5 id reports `supports_temperature=False` and a 512 cache minimum; a 5.5 Bedrock request carries `output_config.effort` and no `temperature`; a direct one carries `anthropic_effort`.\n- Edge: the corrected direct profile reports forced tool choice unsupported; an unmapped id keeps family defaults (no effort, temperature kept); `sizing` maps `us.anthropic.claude-haiku-5-5` to `trivial`.\n- Live: provider-parity probe and full run once on 4.x before the change and once on 5.5 after, `AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `git grep -nE 'claude-(opus-4-8|sonnet-4-6|haiku-4-5)' -- rebar.toml .github/llm-providers src/rebar/llm/config.py src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py` prints nothing.\n- [ ] The model-call audit is a ticket comment with one row per call site and API change.\n- [ ] Every incompatibility the audit finds is fixed here or filed as a linked bug.\n- [ ] The capability and settings-builder tests under Testing pass.\n- [ ] The parity probe passes on every 5.5 slot.\n- [ ] The before and after provider-parity results are a ticket comment, and the 5.5 run reports `invalid: false`.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794256039790943001,"uuid":"d6c05322-0e0c-4272-b8c3-6fbba388cc48"}